workedExample:
1. B is never on a right side: in every key.
2. B alone is not a key, so try B plus one attribute:

```formula
B⁺ = {B}
{A, B}⁺ = {A, B, C, D}
{B, C}⁺ = {A, B, C, D}
{B, D}⁺ = {A, B, C, D}
{C, D}⁺ = {A, C, D}
where
B⁺, {A, B}⁺, {B, C}⁺, {B, D}⁺, {C, D}⁺: attribute closures under F = {AB → C, C → D, D → A}
A, B, C, D: the attributes of R
AB: the set {A, B}
→: functionally determines
{ }: a set
In words: AB uses AB → C then C → D; BC uses C → D then D → A; BD uses D → A then AB → C. Without B nothing reaches B, so CD fails.
```

3. All three are minimal, since B alone fails.
4. **3 keys**, and every attribute is prime, which will matter for 3NF.
